NAME
       apropos - search the short descriptions of the manual pages

SYNOPSIS
       apropos KEYWORD

DESCRIPTION
       apropos looks for KEYWORD in the NAME line of every manual page and
       prints each match as "name (section) - description". Upper and lower
       case do not matter. It is the same as man -k KEYWORD.

       Use it when you know what you want to do but not which program does
       it. The search uses a database built by mandb; on a freshly installed
       system run mandb once (as root) if apropos finds nothing.

EXAMPLES
       Find programs that deal with logical volumes:

           apropos "logical volume"

       Find the pages that talk about SELinux contexts:

           apropos context

SEE ALSO
       man(1), whatis(1), mandb(8)
